{"parentUuid":"2cb11b15-5d31-49ab-bb81-1359776c08be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZhKsWTbf79ja56GyQe8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Bastion window is off your current screen again, so you are probably working. I won't take over your screen.\n\nThe push went through (`4b46dca`).\n\n**Where A4 stands:**\n- **The line-comment loop works.** `calc.py:5` asked for the docstring, and the next diff has it.\n- **One fix is still uncommitted.** Restoring `test_add` is in the VM but not committed, and the review flags it under \"Not committed, so it will not land\". If you approve now, the landed change deletes `test_add`.\n- **Open: send back once more, then land.** I need about two minutes in the Bastion window to send `divide` back with \"commit `test_calc.py`\", approve the result, and land it in `demo-b`.\n\n**What this run showed about the harness:**\n- Agent reports can claim work the commits don't contain, so the diff, not the report, is the ground truth.\n- gpt-5-mini sometimes ends a turn by announcing its next step instead of taking it.\n- `bash -lc` hangs in the VM, and tool calls had no timeout, so one turn stalled for about 25 minutes.\n\nThe turn guide now covers all three. They are also the first concrete checks A5's constraints should enforce: commit everything, never delete existing tests, and leave a clean tree at build end. A6's evals should measure them.\n\nTell me when the screen is free, or press \"Send back\" with that note yourself and I'll take it from there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_read_input_tokens":866978,"output_tokens":565,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":107},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":309,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":866978,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":309},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"54992cc0-a430-4938-bede-61c00232b8ef","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZhKs97yajM7M7GeP2UG","attributionMcpServer":"cmux-cua","attributionMcpTool":"list_windows","type":"assistant","uuid":"22617f18-8ebc-4944-a820-d23ea24fd0a1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T04:37:49.032Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main"}
