{"parentUuid":"1d31a472-a139-4948-93cd-8555b5c5aae1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZicegMyY4iwUEo5P1me","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right: the `divide` job is gone, but not because it was deleted. When I approved it, the land failed. The bundle out of the VM named `HEAD` instead of the branch, so the worktree pull found no branch to merge. Back then, a failed land also stopped the VM, which threw away its commits. The job is now under Finished as failed, and `demo-b` was never changed.\n\n**Fixed and committed** (the push is still running in the background):\n- The bundle now names the branch. I tested the round trip with real git.\n- A failed land no longer stops the job. It keeps the VM and its commits and waits for you: Approve retries the land, and Stop ends the job. The job page shows \"The land failed; the VM and its commits are kept\". A core test covers it, bringing the core to 24 tests.\n\n**To finish the A4 exit**, I approved the `subtract` plan in `demo-a`, and its build is running now. When it reaches Review, I'll approve it and confirm the land in `demo-a`'s main branch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":874,"cache_read_input_tokens":788961,"output_tokens":326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":874,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":326,"cache_read_input_tokens":788961,"cache_creation_input_tokens":874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":874},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee