{"parentUuid":"6f02c52d-f31e-4992-b157-ddd8ee79ee6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZipkMGsTVzKLhDAXMG7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012vJiNtipycHFphL6eg5CsW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold=[l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('| A4 |')][0]\nnew=\"| A4 | done | The diff, captured from the VM after each build and shown per file with line comments (e5da6d7). The checkpoint dial: ask, hold and auto, review never below hold, holds resumed after a restart (0bdb745). Turn guide and uncommitted-work flag (4b46dca). Landing fixes: the bundle names the branch, a failed land waits on the owner with its VM, and the land passes `target_branch`. 24 core tests, 29 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), driven in the window: on `divide`, line comments on `calc.py:5` and `test_calc.py:3` came back verbatim and each next diff answered them; on `subtract`, the owner approved the plan and the review, the land failed once on `target_checked_out_dirty` (an untracked `__pycache__` in the target) and waited, and Approve retried it: `demo-a` main got `0e30e2f`, both tests pass, and the VM is gone. Not run live: a hold expiring (30 min); the core and loop tests cover it. |\"\ns=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace(\"| A5 to A13 | — | — |\",\"| A5 | next | — |\\n| A6 to A13 | — | — |\")\na=\"\"\"- Page reads overlap when pushes come fast, so each page keeps only its latest\n  read. An artifact is written before the page hears of a change, so a panel\n  that mounts on that change sees it.\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n\n**What A4 found:**\n\n- An agent's report can claim work its commits do not hold. The diff from the\n  VM is the ground truth, and work left uncommitted is listed at review.\n- gpt-5-mini sometimes ended a turn by announcing its next step, ran tests\n  through `bash -lc` (which hung the VM call), and passed no timeout, so one\n  turn stalled for about 25 minutes. `harness` has no way to stop a turn. The\n  turn guide now covers all three, and A5's constraints should enforce them:\n  commit every change, keep existing tests, leave a clean tree.\n- `git bundle create … HEAD` names no branch, so the pull found nothing. The\n  bundle names the branch now.\n- `worktree::land` needs `target_branch`, refuses a dirty target, and reports\n  through `worktree::land-blocked` with a `reason`.\n- A hidden webview can miss pushes, so the window reloads every page when it\n  regains focus.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"Close A4: land to the workspace's branch, reload pages on focus\n\nPass target_branch to worktree::land, show no artifact at a failed land, and\nread every page again when the window regains focus.\" && echo committed","description":"Update the plan and commit A4","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":813062,"output_tokens":1263,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1110,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1263,"cache_read_input_tokens":813062,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1110},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012vJiNtipycHFphL6eg5CsW":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold=[l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('| A4 |')][0]\nnew=\"| A4 | done | The diff, captured from the VM after each build and shown per file with line comments (e5da6d7). The checkpoint dial: ask, hold and auto, review never below hold, holds resumed after a restart (0bdb745). Turn guide and uncommitted-work flag (4b46dca). Landing fixes: the bundle names the branch, a failed land waits on the owner with its VM, and the land passes `target_branch`. 24 core tests, 29 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), driven in the window: on `divide`, line comments on `calc.py:5` and `test_calc.py:3` came back verbatim and each next diff answered them; on `subtract`, the owner approved the plan and the review, the land failed once on `target_checked_out_dirty` (an untracked `__pycache__` in the target) and waited, and Approve retried it: `demo-a` main got `0e30e2f`, both tests pass, and the VM is gone. Not run live: a hold expiring (30 min); the core and loop tests cover it. |\"\ns=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace(\"| A5 to A13 | — | — |\",\"| A5 | next | — |\\n| A6 to A13 | — | — |\")\na=\"\"\"- Page reads overlap when pushes come fast, so each page keeps only its latest\n  read. An artifact is written before the page hears of a change, so a panel\n  that mounts on that change sees it.\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n\n**What A4 found:**\n\n- An agent's report can claim work its commits do not hold. The diff from the\n  VM is the ground truth, and work left uncommitted is listed at review.\n- gpt-5-mini sometimes ended a turn by announcing its next step, ran tests\n  through `bash -lc` (which hung the VM call), and passed no timeout, so one\n  turn stalled for about 25 minutes. `harness` has no way to stop a turn. The\n  turn guide now covers all three, and A5's constraints should enforce them:\n  commit every change, keep existing tests, leave a clean tree.\n- `git bundle create … HEAD` names no branch, so the pull found nothing. The\n  bundle names the branch now.\n- `worktree::land` needs `target_branch`, refuses a dirty target, and reports\n  through `worktree::land-blocked` w