{"parentUuid":"c09cee1d-07b6-43da-8b8c-eaaa8d68e550","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZiro1Kc6jwEWJZKLLL9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EX6jkgVhdpmujinvcTm5Gj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48/scratchpad && ls -la $S/phases.md && git show c0c4be2:PLAN.md > $S/plan-before.md && wc -l $S/plan-before.md && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nS='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48/scratchpad'\ns=open(S+'/plan-before.md').read()\n# 1. phases replacement and renumbering, as in c963b33\nstart=s.index(\"#### A4 — Review and landing (M)\")\nend=s.index(\"## 8. Verification rules\")\nhead, tail = s[:start], s[end:]\nmapping={'A5':'A8','A6':'A5','A7':'A9','A8':'A10','A9':'A11','A10':'A12','A11':'A13'}\ndef renum(text):\n    return re.sub(r'\\bA(5|6|7|8|9|10|11)\\b', lambda m: '@@'+mapping['A'+m.group(1)], text).replace('@@','')\ns=renum(head)+open(S+'/phases.md').read()+renum(tail)\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]; s=s.replace(a,b)\n# 2. row moves\nrep(\"| Diffs | app: the adapter reads them from the job's worktree | `worktree` or `ide` (stock) | A4 |\",\"| Diffs | app: the adapter reads them from the job's VM | `iii-sandbox` (stock) | A4 |\")\nrep(\"| Approvals | worker | `approval-gate` (stock) | A4 |\\n| Push, PRs, CI watch, merge | worker | `github` (stock) | A4 |\",\"| Constraints and capabilities: the gate's rules and the ladders | app: `bastion-core`, bound as hooks | `harness` hooks | A5 |\\n| Calls held at `ask` | worker | `approval-gate` (stock) | A5 |\\n| The audit chain | app: one writer, rows in `database` | `database` (stock) | A5 |\\n| A/B evals | app: `bastion-core` compares; runs are jobs | `eval`, `judge` (stock) | A6 |\\n| Accounts and their secrets | worker | `secrets` (stock) | A7 |\\n| Forge: push, PRs, CI watch, merge | worker, one adapter per forge | `github` (stock) | A7 |\\n| Issue trackers as request sources | one adapter per tracker | — | A7 |\")\nrep(\"| Oversight presets: high, medium, low, off | Presets in Settings | A9 |\",\"| Oversight presets: high, medium, low, off | Presets in Settings | A7 |\")\nrep(\"| Constraints: board, detail, forms, three tiers | Constraints pages | A5 |\",\"| Constraints: board, detail, forms, three tiers | Constraints pages, each constraint on a ladder | A5 |\")\nrep(\"| Capabilities: grants per stage | Capabilities page | A5 |\",\"| Capabilities: grants per stage | Capabilities page, each grant on a ladder | A5 |\")\nrep(\"| Settings, with history, versions and restore | Settings page | A9 |\",\"| Settings, with history, versions and restore | Settings page | A7 |\")\nrep(\"| Model and provider per stage, and override per job | Models in Settings, override in the job view | A9 |\",\"| Model and provider per stage, and override per job | Models in Settings, override in the job view | A7 |\")\nrep(\"| The vault | The `secrets` worker | A9 |\",\"| The vault | The `secrets` worker | A7 |\")\nrep(\"| Evals: grade and backtest | Evals page | A10 |\",\"| Evals: grade and backtest | A/B evals of harness configurations | A6 |\")\nrep(\"| Accounts, GitHub sign-in, org check, roles | Not ported: one owner (D11) | — |\",\"| Accounts, GitHub sign-in, org check, roles | The owner's own accounts with other services (A7); no sign-in and no roles (D11) | A7 |\")\n# 3. take the tail after the D19 row and join it to the current head (which has the intro, goals, D20-D23)\ni=s.index(\"| D19 |\"); j=s.index(\"\\n\", i)\ntail=s[j+1:]\ncur=open('/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md').read()\nassert cur.rstrip().endswith(\"|\"), cur[-200:]\ns=cur.rstrip(\"\\n\")+\"\\n\"+tail\n# 4. progress rows\nold=[l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('| A4 |')][0]\ns=s.replace(old,\"| A4 | done | The diff, captured from the VM after each build and shown per file with line comments (e5da6d7). The checkpoint dial: ask, hold and auto, review never below hold, holds resumed after a restart (0bdb745). Turn guide and uncommitted-work flag (4b46dca). Landing fixes: the bundle names the branch, a failed land waits on the owner with its VM, and the land passes `target_branch` (75adbe2, f2898c6). 24 core tests, 29 app tests. Live exit (2026-10-31), driven in the window: on `divide`, line comments on `calc.py:5` and `test_calc.py:3` came back verbatim and each next diff answered them; on `subtract`, the owner approved the plan and the review, the land failed once on `target_checked_out_dirty` (an untracked `__pycache__` in the target) and waited, and Approve retried it: `demo-a` main got `0e30e2f`, both tests pass, and the VM is gone. Not run live: a hold expiring (30 min); the core and loop tests cover it. |\")\nrows=[l for l in s.splitlines() if re.match(r'^\\| A(5|6|7|8|9|1[0-3])', l) or l.startswith('| A5 to') or l.startswith('| A8 to')]\nfor r in rows: s=s.replace(r+\"\\n\",\"\")\ns=s.replace(new_a4:= [l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('| A4 |')][0], new_a4+\"\\n| A5 | next | — |\\n| A6 to A13 | — | — |\")\na=\"\"\"- Page reads overlap when pushes come fast, so each page keeps only its latest\n  read. An artifact is written before the page hears of a change, so a panel\n  that mounts on that change sees it.\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n\n**What A4 found:**\n\n- An agent's report can claim work its commits do not hold. The diff from the\n  VM is the ground truth, and work left uncommitted is listed at review.\n- gpt-5-mini sometimes ended a turn by announcing its next step, ran tests\n  through `bash -lc` (which hung the VM call), and passed no timeout, so one\n  turn stalled for about 25 minutes. `harness` has no way to stop a turn. The\n  turn guide now covers all three, and A5's constraints should enforce them:\n  commit every change, keep existing tests, leave a clean tree.\n- `git bundle create … HEAD` names no branch, so the pull found nothing. The\n  bundle names the branch now.\n- `worktree::land` needs `target_branch`, refuses a dirty target, and reports\n  through `worktree::land-blocked` with a `reason`.\n- A hidden webview can miss pushes, so the window reloads every page when it\n  regains focus.\"\"\")\nopen('/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\nwc -l PLAN.md; grep -n \"^## \\|^### \\|^#### \" PLAN.md | cut -c1-60; grep -n \"^| A[0-9]\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-50","description":"Rebuild the truncated plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":816288,"output_tokens":3464,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":695},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":218,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3464,"cache_read_input_tokens":816288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":218},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EX6jkgVhdpmujinvcTm5Gj":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48/scratchpad && ls -la $S/phases.md && git show c0c4be2:PLAN.md > $S/plan-before.md && wc -l $S/plan-before.md && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nS='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/135a2369-1f42-433b-aacc-5c1b0ce18b48/scratchpad'\ns=open(S+'/plan-before.md').read()\n# 1. phases replacement and renumbering, as in c963b33\nstart=s.index(\"#### A4 — Review and landing (M)\")\nend=s.index(\"## 8. Verification rules\")\nhead, tail = s[:start], s[end:]\nmapp