{"parentUuid":"1bf08d1c-0fc9-4403-9ce3-0890f2bb30d2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a1601cc2-bdb1-489e-8288-075aa8dccf5b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kj1NGxguJtg4F1iH5Li9dN","type":"tool_result","content":" `harness::send` for a wake or a sub-agent, anything else for a mechanical reaction.One declared condition. Evaluated at fire time with the typed decision contract; ordinary iii functions, so a barrier or a claim is just a function someone wrote.Working-directory root stamped onto the first turn of a session whose send carries no explicit `fs_scope.root`; `null` when defaulting is disabled (`default_filesystem_root: \"off\"`) or neither `III_COMPOSE_DIR` nor the cwd is available.Effective per-session boundary for shell/coder calls: the configured `filesystem_boundary`, or under `auto`, `workspace` when the filesystem approval hook can widen it, otherwise `configured_roots`.The engine's own trigger id (absent only in the brief window before the engine acknowledged the registration).The function a fire calls. Absent for a wake \n or report it pending.harness::function::resolveInternal: settle a pending call's result (or release a held call) and resume the parked turn.harness::stopRequest cancellation of an in-flight turn (cascades to spawned children).harness::statusRead a session's current turn. Returns a lean summary by default; pass verbose: true for the full runtime report and untruncated result.harness::system-prompt::getPreview the system prompt layers a session will use without making a model request.harness::context-policyReturn the Harness context-pruning policy for a destination model without making a model request.harness::session-treeRead the durable root-and-descendant session tree for one harness run.Aggregate durable model usage, function outcomes, and available trace/span observability for the session tree `root_session_id` belongs to (`session_id` is accepted as an alias, and a sub-agent id is resolved to its root). `complete` is true only after every session in the durable tree has reached a terminal turn. Pass `omit_context: true` when you only need the counters and cost: each session's context snapshot is then left out.harness::teardownInternal control-plane: remove trigger bindings owned by a root harness session tree.List the trigger bindings a session owns: subscription id, trigger type/config, target (absent = notifies the owner), label, conditions, lifecycle, and fire count. In-turn calls may omit `session_id`.Tear down one trigger binding by subscription id (engine trigger and durable record); a still-armed wake notifies its parked owner. `session_id` must name the owner; in-turn calls may omit it.Internal control-plane: remove a still-parked queued message by entry_id (the console's edit-queued path).harness::edit_queuedInternal control-plane: edit a still-parked queued message in place by entry_id, preserving its queue position.harness::filesystem::grantInternal control-plane: grant a session access to an additional filesystem root.harness::filesystem::grantsInternal control-plane: list additional filesystem roots granted to a session.harness::filesystem::revokeInternal control-plane: revoke a session's access to an additional filesystem root.harness::filesystem::infoInternal control-plane: the default working-directory root new sessions are scoped to.harness::projects::listInternal control-plane: list the operator's durable project catalog.harness::projects::upsertInternal control-plane: remember, touch, or rename a project directory.harness::projects::deleteInternal control-plane: remove a project directory from the durable catalog.harness::sweep-pendingInternal cron sweep: resolve pending function calls past their timeout and re-enqueue the step of running turns left without one, so a turn never wedges; then move finished turn records' inline prompts to shared bodies and delete unused bodies. Not called directly.harness::on-session-deletedInternal: drop a deleted session's ephemeral subscriptions. Not called directly.all harness::* functions registered\n the registration SUCCEEDED, but its wiring looks suspicious (e.g. a turn-event filter naming a session that doesn't exist). Read it and fix the wiring if it applies.Agent-facing unsubscribe contract. The id is the harness subscription id returned by [`SubscribeResponse`], not the underlying engine binding id.UnsubscribeArgsTrigger type to listen on: `cron`, `state`, `stream`, `timer`, or another worker's custom type (e.g. `database::row-changed`).Trigger config passed verbatim to the engine, a JSON object: cron `{ \"expression\" }`, state scope/key, timer `{ \"in_ms\" }` or `{ \"at\" }` (epoch ms).A short human label echoed back in the notification text.Auto-unsubscribe after the first fire; defaults to true for a wake (no `function_id`) and `timer`, false for a call binding and `cron`.Function called on each event; omit to be notified in this session instead. `harness::spawn` is never a valid target.Optional `{ action?, payload?, event_into? }`: user-facing event text, the fixed call payload, and the JSON pointer where the event is injected into it.Long form of `function_id` + `metadata`: `{ function_id, payload?, event_into? }`.Fire-time gates, in order; each is an iii function answering `{ decision: \"allow\" | \"skip\", payload?, reason? }`.When the binding stops firing; top-level `once` is the shorthand.Agent-facing subscription contract.SubscribeArgs\n the sweep scans all turn records). A struct keeps the request schema concrete.`deliver` (default) supplies the result; `execute` releases a hook-held call through the remaining trigger pipeline.execute only: one-shot additional roots trusted by the caller and unioned with the session's durable filesystem grants.False when the call is unknown, already done, or (execute) not held.True when this resolve re-enqueued the turn.`session::deleted` payload (only the field we read).Omit to stop the current turn.struct SweepEventstruct ResolveFsScopestruct FunctionResolveRequeststruct SessionDeletedEventstruct StopRequeststruct TeardownRequestV1assertion failed: previnconsistent in dropTraceFlagsSpanContextspan_idtrace_flagsis_remotetrace_state\ncalled `Result::unwrap()` on an `Err` valueharness::delete-session-treeDurably cancel and delete only the selected session subtree; returns an operation snapshot.harness::delete-session-tree-statusRead a durable session subtree deletion snapshot, or null if unknown.Internal queued subtree deletion continuation.Entry point: ensure the session, persist the incoming message, and kick off a turn; returns fast (or merges into a running turn).Compact a session's conversation now and wait for the outcome: summarise its older history with the session's (or the named) model, keep the recent tail verbatim, and tell every client watching the session. `/compact` through harness::send starts the same compaction without waiting.Spawn a sub-agent in a child session (never a trigger target) and return { child_session_id, child_turn_id } immediately; the child's outcome reaches you only through whatever destination its task names. Check `harness::status` for child health; children are leaves unless options.orchestrator is true.harness::askAsk the user for a decision between discrete options: 1-4 questions, 2-4 options each; the UI adds a free-text \"Other\" choice, so do not include one. The questions are shown as a clickable card in the chat, your turn ends, and the answer arrives as the user's next message, so do not repeat the questions in text. Not available to sub-agents or structured-output turns.Internal fire handler for a harness-registered trigger binding: evaluates the binding's conditions, projects the event into the target's payload, and dispatches it (a wake into the owner session, or a plain function call). Never called directly \ndecision\ninternally tagged enum DecisionAssembleOutputsystem_promptmessagestoken_countusableeffective_max_output_tokensappliedbreakdownByRoleTokensuserassistantfunction_resultcustomAppliedinitial_token_countprunedcompactedsummarytail_start_indextokens_beforesummarized_head_tokensCountTokensOutputtokensby_rolestatusinternally tagged enum CompactOutputCompactOutputEmptyAssembleBreakdownsystem_prompt_tokenstools_tokensby_partestimatorallowskipokbusyemptyoverflowTriggerRequest.namespaceiii.tag.hiddenINVALID_SCOPEiii-rust-sdkharness::state::compare-and-set\nstatefunction_idchild_turn_idchild_session_reusedheld_byheld_argumentsreconciledpending_timeout_mspending_atfunction_call_idcontract_digestsource_function_call_idsource_content_digesteligiblerepeatserror_digestcountuser_turnsusagetotalturnsfolded_sessionsmodel_callstool_callsinput_tokensoutput_tokenscache_read_tokenscache_write_tokensskillstoolshook_guidanceestimatorusableeffective_max_output_tokenscategoriescompactedsummarized_head_tokensprompt_surface_digestprompt_sections_fallbackprefix_divergencestimestampindexcall_idcauseprovider_notecache_readassistantfunction_resultcustomrootspayloadresult_intoretry_prompttimeout_msmessageoriginqueued_atunknown_skillsskills_indexinheritance_errorroot_session_idused_tokensreserved_tokensmax_cost_microusdused_cost_microusdreserved_cost_microusdevent_intoconfigmax_firesexpires_atregistered_by_turntrigger_idownertargetconditionslifecyclecapabilitycausationdedup_keyfiresinputcache_writereasoningeffortdescriptiondisplay_namecontext_windowinput_limitsupports_thinkingsupports_xhighsupports_thinking_offreasoning_effortssupports_toolssupports_visionsupports_cachesupports_structured_outputpricingdefault_modeldefault_thinking_leveltokensby_roleforked_fromnext_cursorcustom_type__bindingoperation_idattemptdeleted_session_idserrormembersplannedsystem_prompt_strategyorchestratormax_childrenfilesystem_rootdisplayparent_session_idgroupsvaluetrace_idsspan_countfirst_seen_mslast_seen_msduration_mserror_counttrigger_typelabelexpires_in_msfewer elements in mapmap with a single keystring or mapstepfreeuserkindtaskask_stepsessionsby_modeloutcomesfirst_atoverheadprev_lenpriorityon_errorsnapshotdeadlinenotifiedassertion failed: match track_edge_idx {\nsub-agent display always serializesmessageevent src/config.rs:238harness::configsrc/config.rsevent src/config.rs:245event src/subagent.rs:724harness::subagentsrc/subagent.rsevent src/config.rs:365varevent src/policy.rs:170harness::policypatternsrc/policy.rsevent src/policy.rs:179harness::context_snapshot::PrefixDivergenceV11-4 questions shown together on one card; the answer arrives as the user's next message, one line per question.Short chip label such as `Approach`, 1-16 characters; prefixes the answer line (`Approach: <label>`).The full question text shown above the options.Let the user pick several options (checkboxes) instead of one.2-4 discrete choices; do not add an \"Other\" option, the UI adds a free-text one.harness::ask::AskQuestionThe choice as the user sees and sends it, 1-80 characters, unique within its question.Optional one-line explanation shown under the label.harness::ask::AskOptionThe card is shown; the answer arrives as the user's next message.The function-call id of this ask.The turn that asked; once the session's current turn differs, the question has been answered.The questions as shown, in request order.What an accepted ask records as its result `details`: the card the UI draws and the ids it uses to tell an open question from an answered one.harness::state::QueuedMessageDispatch arguments exactly as the model wrote them.Lossless repairs only: parse stringified JSON the schema rejects.`coerce`, then ask the judge worker (when deployed) about the rest.How [`WorkerConfig::call_reconciliation`] repairs malformed call arguments.Default per-turn generate-step cap when a send omits `max_turns`.Default wait guard for a parked pending call (sub-agent / hook hold) before the sweep resolves it with an error. Milliseconds.Sub-agent depth budget: `harness::spawn` past this is refused.Fan-out budget: child sessions created by a turn past this are refused; appending work to an existing eligible session does not consume a slot.Output-contract validation retries before a best-effort finalise.Mid-stream transient provider/router failures to resume from the preserved transcript before the turn is marked failed. Transport retries remain owned by llm-router.Capture-time byte cap on a function result (`content` + `details`); over it, an elision marker replaces the result. 0 disables, values under 1 KiB are raised to 1 KiB (MOT-4498).Send the system prompt to `router::chat` as `system_sections` (the frozen profile/identity prefix, then the per-session context) plus a `cache_intent` digest, so cache-aware providers can route every session on the same profile to one prefix entry \nSynchronous hook: first step of a turn, before any model spend. May veto.Synchronous hook: after context assembly, before generation. May extend the system prompt, append messages, or veto. Static-only bindings may declare their exact contribution as metadata.inject_prompt; it joins the prompt before assembly.Synchronous hook: after the final assistant message update. Observe only.Synchronous hook: after the allow/deny policy passes, before the target is invoked. May deny, hold, or rewrite arguments.Synchronous hook: after the target returns, before the result is appended. May rewrite content/details/is_error.Synchronous hook: at finalize, after the output contract validated the result, before the turn completes. Deny re-prompts the turn (bounded by max_validation_retries). Config `sessions` globs scope it; config `payload`+`result_into` bind a plain composition function (fp::pipe) as the validator.checked aboveshell::execapproval::filesystem-access-watchregistered the six harness::hook::* trigger types\nTurnStatusrunningawaiting_functionscompletedcancelledfailedExposeModeagent_triggernativeFunctionPolicyallowdenyexposeSkillContextfilterbaselinebaseline_refTurnRecordturn_idsession_idstatusstepturn_countdepth