6 characters; prefixes the answer line (`Approach: <label>`).The full question text shown above the options.Let the user pick several options (checkboxes) instead of one.2-4 discrete choices; do not add an \"Other\" option, the UI adds a free-text one.harness::ask::AskQuestionThe choice as the user sees and sends it, 1-80 characters, unique within its question.Optional one-line explanation shown under the label.harness::ask::AskOptionThe card is shown; the answer arrives as the user's next message.The function-call id of this ask.The turn that asked; once the session's current turn differs, the question has been answered.The questions as shown, in request order.What an accepted ask records as its result `details`: the card the UI draws and the ids it uses to tell an open question from an answered one.harness::state::QueuedMessageDispatch arguments exactly as the model wrote them.Lossless repairs only: parse stringified JSON the schema rejects.`coerce`, then ask the judge worker (when deployed) about the rest.How [`WorkerConfig::call_reconciliation`] repairs malformed call arguments.Default per-turn generate-step cap when a send omits `max_turns`.Default wait guard for a parked pending call (sub-agent / hook hold) before the sweep resolves it with an error. Milliseconds.Sub-agent depth budget: `harness::spawn` past this is refused.Fan-out budget: child sessions created by a turn past this are refused; appending work to an existing eligible session does not consume a slot.Output-contract validation retries before a best-effort finalise.Mid-stream transient provider/router failures to resume from the preserved transcript before the turn is marked failed. Transport retries remain owned by llm-router.Capture-time byte cap on a function result (`content` + `details`); over it, an elision marker replaces the result. 0 disables, values under 1 KiB are raised to 1 KiB (MOT-4498).Send the system prompt to `router::chat` as `system_sections` (the frozen profile/identity prefix, then the per-session context) plus a `cache_intent` digest, so cache-aware providers can route every session on the same profile to one prefix entry \nSynchronous hook: first step of a turn, before any model spend. May veto.Synchronous hook: after context assembly, before generation. May extend the system prompt, append messages, or veto. Static-only bindings may declare their exact contribution as metadata.inject_prompt; it joins the prompt before assembly.Synchronous hook: after the final assistant message update. Observe only.Synchronous hook: after the allow/deny policy passes, before the target is invoked. May deny, hold, or rewrite arguments.Synchronous hook: after the target returns, before the result is appended. May rewrite content/details/is_error.Synchronous hook: at finalize, after the output contract validated the result, before the turn completes. Deny re-prompts the turn (bounded by max_validation_retries). Config `sessions` globs scope it; config `payload`+`result_into` bind a plain composition function (fp::pipe) as the validator.checked aboveshell::execapproval::filesystem-access-watchregistered the six harness::hook::* trigger types\nTurnStatusrunningawaiting_functionscompletedcancelledfailedExposeModeagent_triggernativeFunctionPolicyallowdenyexposeSkillContextfilterbaselinebaseline_refTurnRecordturn_idsession_idstatusstepturn_countdepthmessage_previewabortwatermark_entry_idstream_request_idoptionscallsparentdisplay_parent_session_idfunctions_acknowledgedfunction_contract_ledgerfailed_callsskill_ackskills_startedcontext_snapshotpre_generate_hook_tokensresultresult_errorstop_reasondispatch_only_functionsvalidation_retriestransient_resumesask_stepask_seen_stepcreated_atupdated_atIdemRecordentry_idtsSkillAckgenerationfingerprintidsAgentIdentityidnameiconcolorResponseLanguagecodeTurnOptionsmodelprovidersystem_promptsystem_prompt_refskills_promptskill_contextmax_turnsmax_output_tokensmax_total_tokensmax_cost_usdbudget_root_session_idthinking_levelpro